#lang rhombus
// The slow suites in one process: the standard theories are replayed once
// (about 3.5 minutes) instead of once per suite. The order matters. The
// golden suites compare against the logical state after define.ml, so they
// run before the upstream tests, which define new constants of their own.
// Each suite also runs on its own (`raco test tests/golden/hol_light.rhm`).
// upstream/lagrange_lemma.rhm is not here: its quotations are read against
// the theories up to real.ml, and with every theory loaded `a + b - c` is
// typed differently, so REAL_ARITH fails. It runs in a process of its own.
import:
  "../golden/hol_light.rhm"
  "../golden/printer.rhm"
  "../upstream/basic_tests.rhm"
  "../upstream/dickson.rhm"
